  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Capacity of Thailand to Combat Trafficking in Persons and Smuggling of Migrants through Enhanced Border Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201C;Enhancing the Capacity of Thailand to Combat Trafficking in Persons and Smuggling of Migrants through Enhanced Border Management&#x201D; project will complement existing IOM programmes, including an ongoing initiative that has contributed to the establishment of the NRM. IOM continues to support the Royal Thai Government (RTG) in preventing and prosecuting human trafficking, as well as enhancing protection services for VOTs.  This includes supporting the operationalization of the NRM at the local level. The project will enable IOM to provide a more integrated and comprehensive response by increasing the capacity of law enforcement, particularly TIB, to enhance border management systems and processes through enhanced skills on document examination to prevent and detect human trafficking and migrant smuggling and contribute to enhanced prosecution of this transnational crime. 
 
The project will further enhance inter-ministerial collaboration including cooperation with the Ministry of Social Development and Human Security (MSDHS) and the multi-disciplinary teams established as part of the NRM and engage with protection actors involve the local communities in border areas to increase community members&#x2019; awareness and resilience against recruitment from transnational organized crime groups.</narrative>
  </description>
